From: Betterr <51264180+Star-caorui@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:53:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Updater: Draw the banner pattern once

The pattern behind the device info card is an AGSL shader that, for
every pixel, tests 135 circles across 9 tiles. drawWithCache keeps the
shader object, but onDrawBehind still runs it over the whole card each
time the card is drawn, and scrolling draws it on every frame.

The pattern only depends on the card size and two colours, so record
it into an offscreen graphics layer when the cache is built and draw
that layer instead. drawWithCache rebuilds it when any of them change.

Scrolling the main screen up and down eight times on a Redmi Note 13 5G
(Dimensity 6080, Mali-G57 MC2, 1080x2400 at 120 Hz):

                 frames  janky   50th / 90th percentile
  before            182  92.3%   81 / 200 ms
  after            1538   0.7%   12 / 13 ms
  before, again     168  97.6%   81 / 200 ms

The preferences screen of the same app takes 5 ms per frame.

Change-Id: I25c3a80584286bf55976e70256992a8db71babb1
---
 .../java/org/lineageos/updater/deviceinfo/UpdaterCard.kt | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/updater/deviceinfo/UpdaterCard.kt b/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/updater/deviceinfo/UpdaterCard.kt
index 2d7795f..7254303 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/updater/deviceinfo/UpdaterCard.kt
+++ b/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/updater/deviceinfo/UpdaterCard.kt
@@ -29,6 +29,8 @@ import androidx.compose.ui.graphics.Color
 import androidx.compose.ui.graphics.ColorFilter
 import androidx.compose.ui.graphics.ShaderBrush
 import androidx.compose.ui.graphics.Shape
+import androidx.compose.ui.graphics.layer.CompositingStrategy
+import androidx.compose.ui.graphics.layer.drawLayer
 import androidx.compose.ui.graphics.toArgb
 import androidx.compose.ui.layout.ContentScale
 import androidx.compose.ui.platform.LocalDensity
@@ -318,8 +320,13 @@ private fun Modifier.updaterHeaderPattern(
     }
     val brush = ShaderBrush(shader)
 
+    val patternLayer = obtainGraphicsLayer().apply {
+        compositingStrategy = CompositingStrategy.Offscreen
+        record { drawRect(brush) }
+    }
+
     onDrawBehind {
-        drawRect(brush)
+        drawLayer(patternLayer)
     }
 }
 
